<!-- ===================== 01 · THE STORY ===================== -->
<section class="section story">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <p class="label label--center" data-reveal="up">the story</p>
    <h2 class="dhead center" style="margin-inline:auto;max-width:16ch;" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="90">
      <b>Architecture that</b><b><em>answers to the weather</em></b>
    </h2>
    <div class="lede" style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="180">
      <p>Every building here is a different argument about how to stay cool, stay warm, and stay quiet.</p>
      <p>Grass-clad caves, cottages raised on stilts and a pyramid of pine — arranged between a swimming pool and the river Falgu.</p>
      <p>The grass-clad cave cottages temper the room to the weather outside. The igloos hold an interior up to ten degrees below the air around them. The pyramid cottages are panelled in pine milled from waste packaging timber, with brick corbelled walls and a slant roof that make them energy efficient.</p>
      <p>Around them: exquisitely designed rooms, organic food, village trails, a swimming pool and a splash pool.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="story__rule" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="260"></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== 02 · THE PLACE ===================== -->
<section class="section section--flush-top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <figure class="frame frame--plx frame--pano" style="margin:0 0 clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4rem)" data-reveal="clip-u">
      <img src="https://www.sambodhiretreat.org/images/Homepage_Resort_INDEX/top-slider-img13.jpg" alt="The grounds at Sambodhi Retreat, Bodhgaya" data-parallax="0.26" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </figure>

    <div class="split">
      <div class="col-5" style="grid-column:span 5;" data-reveal="left">
        <p class="label">bodhgaya</p>
        <h2 class="dhead"><b>The slow part</b><b><em>of the day</em></b></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-7" data-reveal="right">
        <p class="lede">Bodhgaya is where the Buddha attained enlightenment. The retreat sits in that landscape rather than commenting on it.</p>
        <p class="body-copy" style="margin-top:1.3rem;">On one side, the swimming pool. On the other, the river Falgu. From the green cave cottages, a clear view of the Mahabodhi temple. Between them: village trails, organic food, and rooms built to hold their own temperature so the air conditioning has less to argue with.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="tlink" href="accommodations.html">see the rooms
            <svg width="15" height="9" viewBox="0 0 15 9" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 1l4 3.5L10 8M0 4.5h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== 03 · FEATURED PAIR ===================== -->
<section class="section section--flush-top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="shead shead--split">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="label">accommodations</p>
        <h2 class="dhead"><b>Sixty rooms.</b><b><em>No two ideas repeated</em></b></h2>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal="right" style="align-self:end;">
        <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:1.6rem;">Sambodhi Retreat is a boutique hotel of sixty rooms — twelve of them large suites, four of them family rooms.</p>
        <a class="tlink" href="accommodations.html">view accommodations
          <svg width="15" height="9" viewBox="0 0 15 9" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 1l4 3.5L10 8M0 4.5h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feat" data-stagger="130">
      <article class="fcard" data-reveal="clip-u">
        <img src="https://www.sambodhiretreat.org/images/rooms-col1/sambodhi-retreat-bodhgaya-green-caves-1.jpg" alt="Green Cave Cottages" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <div class="fcard__in">
          <h3 class="fcard__name">Green Cave Cottages</h3>
          <p class="fcard__text">Grass-clad, facing the swimming pool with the river Falgu behind, and a clear view of the Mahabodhi temple. Four beds give two couples privacy without dropping the luxury.</p>
          <a class="tlink tlink--light" href="accommodations.html#green-cave">full details
            <svg width="15" height="9" viewBox="0 0 15 9" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 1l4 3.5L10 8M0 4.5h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fcard" data-reveal="clip-u">
        <img src="https://www.sambodhiretreat.org/images/rooms-col1/sambodhi-retreat-bodhgaya-pyramid-cottages-1.jpg" alt="Pyramid Cottage" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <div class="fcard__in">
          <h3 class="fcard__name">Pyramid Cottage</h3>
          <p class="fcard__text">A pyramid-shaped cluster panelled in pine reclaimed from packaging timber. Brick corbelled walls, a slant roof and wood rendering inside make it an energy-efficient unit.</p>
          <a class="tlink tlink--light" href="accommodations.html#pyramid">full details
            <svg width="15" height="9" viewBox="0 0 15 9" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 1l4 3.5L10 8M0 4.5h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

